      "stem": {
        "text": "A ball is projected horizontally at 20 m/s from a height of 45 m. How long does it take to reach the ground? (Take g = 10 m/s².)",
        "inline": []
      },
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "2 s"
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "text": "3 s"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "4.5 s"
        },
        {
          "id": "d",
          "text": "9 s"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "b",
      "explanation": {
        "text": "The vertical motion starts from rest, so h = ½gt² gives 45 = 5t², and t = 3 s. The horizontal speed does not change the time of the fall.",
